WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.890
All right, okay, well,

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:05.818
apparently, our next guest just walked in the door.

3
00:00:05.818 --> 00:00:08.000
That's how it goes here with New York traffic, I guess.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.147
Nothing like leaving it 'til the last minute.

5
00:00:10.147 --> 00:00:13.589
You can find his stand up dates at JonDore.com.

6
00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:14.849
Next week, you can see him

7
00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:17.973
in the Broadway show Hercules: The Musical,

8
00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:19.481
please welcome Jon Dore!

9
00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:22.731
(applause and fanfare)

10
00:00:38.696 --> 00:00:40.196
I'm embarrassed.

11
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.367
I'm clearly trying to fit too much into my days.

12
00:00:47.527 --> 00:00:49.022
It's true what Conan said.

13
00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:52.714
Next week, I am starring in Hercules: The Musical.

14
00:00:52.714 --> 00:00:55.131
I play the role of a centaur,

15
00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:57.812
a mythical creature,

16
00:00:58.862 --> 00:01:00.687
Greek mythology,

17
00:01:00.687 --> 00:01:01.890
and today we had a dress rehearsal,

18
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.761
and it went a little late,

19
00:01:03.761 --> 00:01:07.414
and I did not have time to change.

20
00:01:07.414 --> 00:01:09.286
Gettin' in and out of that Uber was a nightmare,

21
00:01:09.286 --> 00:01:11.533
I'll tell you that much.

22
00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:14.700
My rating's gonna plummet, guaranteed.

23
00:01:15.749 --> 00:01:17.191
And I'm embarrassed, I feel terrible.

24
00:01:17.191 --> 00:01:18.231
I feel bad for Conan,

25
00:01:18.231 --> 00:01:20.388
I feel bad for you people, the viewers at home.

26
00:01:20.388 --> 00:01:22.768
I mean, I'm supposed to tell jokes,

27
00:01:22.768 --> 00:01:26.226
and this is gonna be distracting, so--

28
00:01:26.226 --> 00:01:28.308
I mean, if there's any way

29
00:01:28.308 --> 00:01:32.232
you guys could just maybe not focus on how I look,

30
00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:34.950
and just pay attention to what I'm saying,

31
00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.248
I think everything will work out.

32
00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:37.107
What do you say?

33
00:01:37.107 --> 00:01:37.940
Will you--

34
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.308
(applause)

35
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:41.544
Oh, thank you, all right!

36
00:01:41.544 --> 00:01:43.000
Lets have some fun!

37
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.600
Here we are at the Apollo!

38
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.433
Whoo!

39
00:01:47.562 --> 00:01:48.812
Apollo Theater!

40
00:01:50.214 --> 00:01:52.280
Harlem, New York!

41
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.767
(applause)

42
00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.418
Yeah, oh, yeah!

43
00:01:55.418 --> 00:01:56.418
There we go!

44
00:01:58.212 --> 00:01:59.045
Joke one.

45
00:02:03.283 --> 00:02:05.520
You know, there was a time in my life

46
00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.432
when I started hanging around the wrong crowd,

47
00:02:08.432 --> 00:02:12.599
and then one day I just realized, "Wait a minute."

48
00:02:12.759 --> 00:02:16.009
"I don't recognize any of these people."

49
00:02:18.254 --> 00:02:22.421
"I have literally been hanging around with the wrong crowd."

50
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:25.569
"How long has this been going on?"

51
00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:28.405
But eventually, I started hanging around the right crowd,

52
00:02:28.405 --> 00:02:32.572
and we did a lot of drugs and we shoplifted, so, yeah.

53
00:02:38.243 --> 00:02:40.105
See, that joke usually gets an applause break,

54
00:02:40.105 --> 00:02:41.969
but I feel like the outfit--

55
00:02:41.969 --> 00:02:43.053
(light applause)

56
00:02:43.053 --> 00:02:45.085
Oh, don't, please.

57
00:02:45.085 --> 00:02:46.835
If it's not sincere--

58
00:02:47.787 --> 00:02:49.504
You know what, maybe I'm just gonna skip the jokes,

59
00:02:49.504 --> 00:02:51.349
'cause this is too distracting,

60
00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:52.843
and Conan did promise me that I'd be able

61
00:02:52.843 --> 00:02:54.978
to premiere a song from Hercules: The Musical, so--

62
00:02:54.978 --> 00:02:55.811
(applause)

63
00:02:55.811 --> 00:02:59.521
Yeah, if you don't mind, I'll do that.

64
00:02:59.521 --> 00:03:01.562
Jimmy, whenever you're ready.

65
00:03:01.562 --> 00:03:04.479
(light flute tune)

66
00:03:07.831 --> 00:03:11.914
♫ Oh, Hercules, we need you here

67
00:03:13.811 --> 00:03:17.728
♫ Come down from Mount Olympus

68
00:03:19.687 --> 00:03:23.854
♫ Oh, Hercules, no one thinks you're weird

69
00:03:25.677 --> 00:03:29.594
♫ Come down from Mount Olympus

70
00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:35.411
♫ Oh, Hercules, Her-- ♫

71
00:03:35.624 --> 00:03:38.374
(liquid running)

72
00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.353
(applause and laughter)

73
00:04:11.362 --> 00:04:15.445
(liquid spurting intermittently)

74
00:04:26.584 --> 00:04:29.482
I bet you think I'm embarrassed.

75
00:04:29.482 --> 00:04:32.786
I bet you think I'm humiliated, but I'm not,

76
00:04:32.786 --> 00:04:34.006
'cause it's not what you think.

77
00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.270
That wasn't urine.

78
00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.518
That's right, it's my new energy drink, Integrity.

79
00:04:39.518 --> 00:04:40.764
[Announcer] Integrity!

80
00:04:40.764 --> 00:04:41.597
(thunder)

81
00:04:41.597 --> 00:04:42.680
You got it.

82
00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.814
Integrity's something I got plenty of.

83
00:04:45.814 --> 00:04:47.658
It's from the makers of the All That Top Hat

84
00:04:47.658 --> 00:04:49.360
Chicken Cooker Oven Hat.

85
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.039
When you're trying to squeeze too much into your day,

86
00:04:52.039 --> 00:04:54.588
I suggest you try Integrity.

87
00:04:54.588 --> 00:04:55.468
[Announcer] Integrity!

88
00:04:55.468 --> 00:04:58.070
(thunder)
Wait a minute

89
00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.811
No, no, no, don't, Jon.

90
00:04:59.811 --> 00:05:00.644
Let me get this straight.

91
00:05:00.644 --> 00:05:04.193
I give you a chance to do stand up at the Apollo Theater--

92
00:05:04.193 --> 00:05:05.285
Thank you.

93
00:05:05.285 --> 00:05:07.050
Which is a great honor.
Yes.

94
00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.032
And you use it to do this stupid commercial.

95
00:05:11.032 --> 00:05:13.631
This is disgraceful, and you have no integrity.

96
00:05:13.631 --> 00:05:14.749
[Announcer] Integrity!

97
00:05:14.749 --> 00:05:17.999
No, don't--
(thunder)

98
00:05:20.139 --> 00:05:21.472
You work for me!

99
00:05:23.097 --> 00:05:24.643
Seriously, this is unacceptable.

100
00:05:24.643 --> 00:05:28.810
You arrive late, you look like a fool, you look ridiculous.

101
00:05:31.391 --> 00:05:32.224
I'm sorry.

102
00:05:32.224 --> 00:05:33.772
You know what?

103
00:05:33.772 --> 00:05:35.168
He's right, Conan's right.

104
00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.582
You're always right.

105
00:05:36.582 --> 00:05:39.962
No, I did arrive late, and that's on me,

106
00:05:39.962 --> 00:05:42.770
and I did abuse my power to promote this,

107
00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.189
and I do look ridiculous.

108
00:05:44.189 --> 00:05:46.847
I'll just take this off.

109
00:05:46.847 --> 00:05:48.027
You don't have to take it off.

110
00:05:48.027 --> 00:05:48.860
No, you can leave it on.

111
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.966
It looks ridiculous, and it's coming off.

112
00:05:50.966 --> 00:05:54.383
No, please don't, no one wants to see--

113
00:05:55.595 --> 00:05:56.826
It's unacceptable.

114
00:05:56.826 --> 00:05:57.659
You should go.

115
00:05:57.659 --> 00:05:59.271
All right, I'm outta here.

116
00:05:59.271 --> 00:06:00.351
[Announcer] Integrity!

117
00:06:00.351 --> 00:06:02.518
(thunder)

118
00:06:06.709 --> 00:06:08.557
Jon Dore, ladies and gentlemen.

119
00:06:08.557 --> 00:06:10.779
(applause)

120
00:06:10.779 --> 00:06:13.612
You never know what he's gonna do.

